{
  "info": {
    "name": "Moments & Memories",
    "description": "Every endpoint the product exposes, in the order you would exercise them.\n\nThree realms, and they do not share credentials:\n  • Mobile API  — /api/v1/*        Bearer {{token}}        (a customer)\n  • Admin panel — /admin/v1/*      Bearer {{adminToken}}   (staff, 2FA)\n  • Health      — /health          no auth\n\nTokens are captured automatically by the Tests script on each sign-in request, so run them top to bottom and nothing needs copying by hand.\n\nSign-in codes are SHA-256 in the database and cannot be read back. Either take the code from the inbox, or run:  npm run dev:code -- <email>",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:3000"
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "you@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "admin@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "code",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "totp",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "mfaToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "vaultId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "memoryId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "uploadId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "assetId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "uploadUrl",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "capsuleId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "recipientId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 · Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No auth, and deliberately so: a guard here would make every container fail its health check and roll the deploy back."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /health/ready",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/ready",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "ready"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Readiness: this one touches the database. Use it to confirm the pool is actually up before blaming an endpoint."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 · Mobile API — sign in",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /auth/request-code",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/request-code",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "request-code"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Always 202, for any address.\n\nThat is the whole point: a 404 for unknown addresses would turn this into a way to ask the server whether somebody has an account here. Creating an account and signing in are the same request — there is no separate sign-up."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('202 Accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "pm.test('says nothing about whether the account exists', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.include('If that address');",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('Now get the code: npm run dev:code -- ' + pm.collectionVariables.get('email'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /auth/verify",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{code}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "verify"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Set the `code` variable first.\n\nOne flat 401 for every failure — wrong code, expired code, too many attempts, no code at all. Distinguishing them would tell an attacker which part of the guess was right.\n\nThe token in the response is the only time that value exists outside your client; the database keeps its SHA-256 and nothing else. This script captures it into {{token}}."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', b.token);",
                  "pm.test('returned a session token', () => pm.expect(b.token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "console.log('isNewAccount:', b.isNewAccount, '| expires in days:', b.expiresInDays);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /auth/verify — wrong code (expect 401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"code\": \"000000\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "verify"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Worth running deliberately. Five of these spend the code entirely — the limit is enforced in the database, not here."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The first endpoint that needs an actor. If this works, the whole chain works: bearer token → app_resolve_session → ActorContext → SET LOCAL app.user_id → sixty row-level policies."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /auth/me — no token (expect 401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 · Mobile API — vaults",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /vaults",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Family\",\n  \"type\": \"shared\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vaults",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "vaults"
              ]
            },
            "description": "type: personal | shared | legacy\n\nTwo writes in one transaction — the vault and the owner's membership row — so a vault with no members cannot exist."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('vaultId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /vaults",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vaults",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "vaults"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /vaults/debug/row-counts",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vaults/debug/row-counts",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "vaults",
                "debug",
                "row-counts"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Proof that the boundary belongs to the database rather than to a handler: the counts are what THIS actor can see, not what the tables hold."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 · Mobile API — archive",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /vaults/:vaultId/memories",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Aaji at the wedding\",\n  \"note\": \"She wore the green sari.\",\n  \"occurredAt\": \"1974-03-14T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"occurredPrecision\": \"year\",\n  \"clientId\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vaults/{{vaultId}}/memories",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "vaults",
                "{{vaultId}}",
                "memories"
              ]
            },
            "description": "occurredAt is when it HAPPENED, not when it was uploaded — defaulting it to now is how a scanned 1974 photograph ends up filed under the Tuesday somebody digitised it.\n\noccurredPrecision: exact | day | month | year | decade\n\nclientId is the device's own id and makes a retry idempotent. {{$guid}} generates a fresh one; paste a fixed value instead to watch deduplicated flip to true."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('memoryId', b.id);",
                  "console.log('deduplicated:', b.deduplicated);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /vaults/:vaultId/memories",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vaults/{{vaultId}}/memories?limit=50",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "vaults",
                "{{vaultId}}",
                "memories"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "50"
                },
                {
                  "key": "before",
                  "value": "",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Keyset pagination, not offset: an offset shifts under you when somebody adds a memory mid-scroll, and this timeline is appended to constantly. Pass nextBefore back as `before`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /uploads",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"memoryId\": \"{{memoryId}}\",\n  \"filename\": \"photo.jpg\",\n  \"contentType\": \"image/jpeg\",\n  \"bytes\": 2400000,\n  \"kind\": \"image\",\n  \"clientId\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/uploads",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "uploads"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns a URL you PUT the file to DIRECTLY. The bytes never pass through this server.\n\n`bytes` must match the file exactly — ContentLength is signed into the URL, so R2 rejects a body of a different size. kind: image | video | audio.\n\nThe quota is checked here, before a byte moves."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('uploadId', b.uploadId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('uploadUrl', b.url);",
                  "console.log('PUT the file to the url in uploadUrl, then run Complete.');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "PUT the file to R2 (direct)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "image/jpeg"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "file",
              "file": {
                "src": ""
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{uploadUrl}}"
            },
            "description": "Body → binary → select your file. It must be the SAME file whose size you declared, or R2 refuses the signature.\n\nNote there is no Authorization header: the signature in the URL is the credential, which is the whole reason this can go straight to Cloudflare."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 from R2', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /uploads/:uploadId/complete",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"kind\": \"image\",\n  \"contentType\": \"image/jpeg\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/uploads/{{uploadId}}/complete",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "uploads",
                "{{uploadId}}",
                "complete"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The server HEADs the object and records the size IT reports, not the one you declared.\n\n409 means the object is not in the bucket — you skipped the PUT, or it failed.\n413 means the object is bigger than the upload was opened for."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('assetId', pm.response.json().assetId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /media/:assetId/url",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/media/{{assetId}}/url",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "media",
                "{{assetId}}",
                "url"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A signed GET, 300 seconds. That TTL is the bound on how long a revoked share can still be opened, which is why it is capped at 900 in the schema rather than left to taste.\n\nOpen the url in a browser to see the file. Strip the query string and it fails — the bucket is private."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('short-lived', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().expiresInSeconds).to.be.at.most(900));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3b · Mobile API — capsules",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /vaults/:vaultId/capsules",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"For your eighteenth\",\n  \"note\": \"You were asleep on my shoulder when I wrote this.\",\n  \"unlockKind\": \"datetime\",\n  \"unlockAt\": \"2044-03-01T09:00:00Z\",\n  \"unlockTimezone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vaults/{{vaultId}}/capsules",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "vaults",
                "{{vaultId}}",
                "capsules"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a DRAFT. unlockAt is when it opens; unlockTimezone is the zone the sender meant, kept separately so a message for a daughter in Pune scheduled from London does not arrive at 03:00 her time.\n\nunlockKind: datetime | milestone | manual"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201',()=>pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('capsuleId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /capsules/:id/recipients",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Aarti\",\n  \"email\": \"aarti@example.com\",\n  \"preferredChannel\": \"email\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/capsules/{{capsuleId}}/recipients",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "capsules",
                "{{capsuleId}}",
                "recipients"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns accessToken ONCE. Only its SHA-256 reaches the database, so a leaked backup does not hand over every sealed message.\n\nHolding it early is harmless — it opens nothing until the capsule is actually delivered."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201',()=>pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b=pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('recipientId', b.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', b.accessToken);",
                  "console.log('Access token captured — it is never returned again.');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /capsules/:id/memories",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"memoryIds\": [\n    \"{{memoryId}}\"\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/capsules/{{capsuleId}}/memories",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "capsules",
                "{{capsuleId}}",
                "memories"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Idempotent — the primary key makes a retry a no-op. Send twice and watch added drop to 0 while total stays the same."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /capsules/:id/seal  ← the moment",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/capsules/{{capsuleId}}/seal",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "capsules",
                "{{capsuleId}}",
                "seal"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Seals the capsule AND schedules its delivery in ONE transaction. A capsule sealed without a job is a promise nothing will ever keep.\n\n400 no recipients · 400 unlock time already passed · 409 already sealed · 403 not the owner\n\nscheduled:false means it was sealed but has no date yet (milestone or manual)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200',()=>pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b=pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('sealed',()=>pm.expect(b.state).to.eql('sealed'));",
                  "pm.test('delivery scheduled',()=>pm.expect(b.scheduled).to.be.true);",
                  "console.log('editable until', b.editableUntil);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "PATCH /capsules/:id — after the grace window (expect 400)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"note\": \"Actually, I changed my mind about all of it.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/capsules/{{capsuleId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "capsules",
                "{{capsuleId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Inside the 15-minute grace window this succeeds. After it, capsule_freeze() raises 23514 and you get 400.\n\nThe freeze is a database trigger, not a check in the handler — it holds for every writer, including an admin tool or a migration script."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /capsules/:id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/capsules/{{capsuleId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "capsules",
                "{{capsuleId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The capsule with its recipients and memories. The access token is NOT here, in any form."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /vaults/:vaultId/capsules",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vaults/{{vaultId}}/capsules?limit=50",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "vaults",
                "{{vaultId}}",
                "capsules"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "50"
                },
                {
                  "key": "state",
                  "value": "sealed",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /open/:token — before delivery (expect 404)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/open/{{accessToken}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "open",
                "{{accessToken}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "NO Authorization header — that is the point. The recipient may have been eleven when this was written and may have no account.\n\nBefore delivery this is 404. A wrong token is the same flat 404, so a bad token learns nothing."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /open/:token — after delivery",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/open/{{accessToken}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "open",
                "{{accessToken}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Works once state is delivered. To try it now, mark it delivered by hand:\n\n  docker exec mm-postgres psql -U postgres -d mm_dev -c \\\"UPDATE capsules SET state='delivered', delivered_at=now() WHERE id='<capsuleId>';\\\"\n\nRecords the FIRST opening only — refresh and firstOpenedAt does not move."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /open/:token/reply",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"body\": \"I read it on the morning of my birthday. Thank you.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/open/{{accessToken}}/reply",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "open",
                "{{accessToken}}",
                "reply"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The reply the sender may never read. Goes through app_post_reply(), which refuses any capsule not delivered or opened."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /capsules/:id/cancel",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/capsules/{{capsuleId}}/cancel",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "capsules",
                "{{capsuleId}}",
                "cancel"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Withdraw the promise. Allowed after sealing, unlike editing: a promise you may silently rewrite is not a promise, but a person must always be able to stop something being sent.\n\nThe job is NOT deleted — the worker completes it without sending, keeping the record that something was scheduled and then withdrawn."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4 · Mobile API — sessions",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /auth/sign-out-others",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/sign-out-others",
