    {
      "name": "5 · Admin panel",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /admin/v1/auth/request-code",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/v1/auth/request-code",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "request-code"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Also always 202, so this cannot be used to enumerate staff.\n\nThe address must already exist in admin_users — there is no self-signup for staff, by design."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "console.log('npm run dev:code -- ' + pm.collectionVariables.get('adminEmail'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /admin/v1/auth/verify-email",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{code}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/v1/auth/verify-email",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "verify-email"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Factor one. The mfaToken it returns can do exactly ONE thing — present a TOTP code. It reaches no other admin route.\n\nOn a first sign-in the response also carries `enrolment`, containing the TOTP secret and otpauth URI. It is shown once and is never recoverable: re-enrolment is refused once a secret exists, because otherwise anybody holding a first-factor token could replace the second factor with one of their own."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('mfaToken', b.mfaToken);",
                  "if (b.enrolment) {",
                  "  console.log('ENROL NOW — shown once:', JSON.stringify(b.enrolment));",
                  "  console.log('Add the otpauth URI to your authenticator app.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /admin/v1/auth/verify-totp",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{mfaToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"{{totp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/v1/auth/verify-totp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "verify-totp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Factor two. Note the Authorization header carries the mfaToken, not a session.\n\nSet `totp` to the six digits from your authenticator. The admin session lasts 8 hours, not the 30 days a customer gets."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', pm.response.json().token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /admin/v1/auth/me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/v1/auth/me",
